  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The National Security Agency (NSA) is a U.S. Department of Defense agency that leads in cybersecurity and signals intelligence (SIGINT), protecting national security systems and providing foreign intelligence to policymakers and military forces. Located in Fort Meade, MD, it collaborates with government, industry, and allies to prevent threats and secure U.S. information.Core Mission & FunctionsSignals Intelligence (SIGINT): Collecting and analyzing foreign signals (communications, radar) to provide intelligence on adversaries.Cybersecurity: Securing U.S. national security systems, information, and the Defense Industrial Base against cyber threats.Combat Support: Acting as a combat support agency, providing intelligence to warfighters.Partnerships: Working with private industry, academia, and allies to improve security.Key ComponentsCentral Security Service (CSS): Coordinates with the NSA to provide cryptologic support.National Security Operations Center (NSOC): Monitors threats 24/7.Careers & EmploymentThe NSA offers careers for professionals in fields such as:Intelligence Analysis: Evaluating foreign data.Language Analysis: Translating foreign intelligence.Engineering and Physical Sciences: Developing technology and cybersecurity tools.Mathematics: Developing secure systems.Requirements to Work at the NSACitizenship: Must be a U.S. citizen.Security Clearance: Must be able to obtain a high-level security clearance.Background Investigation: Must pass a polygraph examination and extensive background check.The agency operates under the authority of the director of national intelligence (DNI) to support foreign intelligence and counterintelligence purposes.",
